\DOC MONOTONE_MAYCHANGE_TAC

\TYPE {MONOTONE_MAYCHANGE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal whose conclusion asserts a composite {MAYCHANGE} relation between
two states, using an assumption asserting a smaller {MAYCHANGE} relation
between the same two states.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments. On a goal {A ?- t} where {t} is a
{MAYCHANGE}-composition (built with {,,}) applied to two state variables, it
discharges the goal using an assumption in {A} of the same shape relating the
same two states, provided the assumed set of changed components is subsumed by
the one in the conclusion. The assumption list is otherwise left untouched.
{
       A ?- t
     ==========  MONOTONE_MAYCHANGE_TAC
}

\FAILURE
Fails when the conclusion is not a {MAYCHANGE} relation between two states at
all (for instance an existentially quantified conclusion about something else),
and when the conclusion is such a relation but no assumption supplies a
matching relation between the same two states that it subsumes — including when
the conclusion mentions component sets not covered by any available assumption.
These failures arise from the matching step inside the tactic.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, the only successful outcome is this complete closing of
the goal.

\ENDDOC
